[INPUT TASK]
"Read the file /tmp/does_not_exist.txt, then if that fails recover by writing
'Recovered content after failure' to /tmp/recovered.txt and confirm it was written."

[EXECUTION TRACE]

Turn 1 — Action: use_tool read_file
  Input:   ("/tmp/does_not_exist.txt")
  Result:  [failure] Error: File does not exist.
  State:   FailureRecord stored. Agent receives readable error observation.
           PeTTa loop does NOT crash — it continues to next turn.

Turn 2 — Agent Reasoning:
  Observation: "File read failed: /tmp/does_not_exist.txt does not exist."
  Decision:    Agent recognizes failure, selects recovery path (write to alternate file).
  Action:      use_tool write_file
  Input:       ("/tmp/recovered.txt", "Recovered content after failure")
  Result:      [success] Successfully wrote file: /tmp/recovered.txt
  State:       Recovery path successful. Failure was NOT silently swallowed.

Turn 3 — Action: use_tool read_file
  Input:   ("/tmp/recovered.txt")
  Result:  [success] Recovered content after failure
  State:   Recovery verified. File written and readable.

Turn 4 — Action: finish
  Content: "Recovery complete:
  1. ❌ read_file '/tmp/does_not_exist.txt' — FAILED: File does not exist.
  2. 🔄 Recovery: Wrote 'Recovered content after failure' to /tmp/recovered.txt
  3. ✅ Verified: Read back confirmed content matches — recovery successful."

[COMPLETION RECORD]
Status:          completed (with recovery)
Turn Count:      4 of 25
Failure Type:    Missing file (tool returns [failure, ...] — no crash)
Recovery Type:   Agent autonomously selects alternate write path
Error Handling:  Failure returned as readable FailureRecord observation

